msgid "``em.write`` — writing, one act one step"
msgstr ""

msgid "Generated for em API |api| from the docstrings of :mod:`s3dgraphy.em.write`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Writing — Transaction → Delta → invoke → guard_write → host.apply (SPEC-plugin §2.3)."
msgstr ""

msgid "**How a transaction makes its delta.** It works on a COPY of the host's graph (made at its first operation) and, at the end, says what changed between the graph and the copy: the new nodes and relations (``nodes``/``edges``), the changed fields (``update_field``), what went away (``remove_node``, ``remove_edge``) — the CRDT's own operations, connector API 1.1. That is what lets the high-level builders CALL THE CORE (``place_landmark``, ``place_extractor``, ``place_reading``, ``combiners.compute``…) instead of rewriting a chain by hand: the core writes on the copy, exactly as it writes everywhere, and the difference is the act. A plugin never writes the chain."
msgstr ""

msgid "Nothing touches the host's graph until the end, and nothing at all when:"
msgstr ""

msgid "the block raises (the exception goes on; nothing applied);"
msgstr ""

msgid "``invoke`` refuses (no author: the host's identity, never an argument);"
msgstr ""

msgid "``guard_write`` refuses (a capability the caller did not declare, a relation the EM language does not allow, a change inside a proposal…) — :class:`~s3dgraphy.em.errors.Refused`, the contract's sentence in EN and IT;"
msgstr ""

msgid "``dry_run=True`` — the delta and the verdict come back, nothing applied."
msgstr ""

msgid "``volatile=True`` is a PROPOSAL (``ingest-batch``): it enters marked ``aux_volatile`` and stays out of the saved document until a person bakes it. A proposal only adds — a change or a removal in it is refused by the seam."
msgstr ""

msgid "Bases: :py:class:`object`"
msgstr ""

msgid "One act: a label, one step. Use it through :func:`write`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Every operation works on a private copy of the graph; the act is applied as one step when the ``with`` block ends without an exception. Nodes can be given by id, by their only name, or as :class:`~s3dgraphy.em.graph.NodeView`."
msgstr ""

